insert into public.moo_versions (id,document_id,label,body_md,change_note,status) values
('21b3dcb4-f37b-5d17-8e66-6763b26ecfbd'::uuid,'b807a5ed-12bb-508f-8a18-0d4f8e599013'::uuid,'v0.1 outline',E'# Area 1. Governance, Organization & Institutional Arrangements\n\n**Part 1: Legal mandate and governance**\n\n> Outline generated from the Inception Report (Annex A) and the Traceability Dictionary v1.1. Drafted chapters that serve this area are listed below; write the remaining procedures here or in a new chapter.\n\n## Scope\n\nCDRRMO/EOC mandate; organizational structure; LDRRMC relationships; authorities; delegation; duty officers; ICS roles; inter-agency coordination; public-private partnerships; accountability.\n\n## MCR2030 alignment\n\n- Primary: Essential 1 – Organize for Disaster Resilience\n- Supporting: Essentials 6, 7, 9\n\n## Drafted chapters for this area\n\n- Introduction: Introduction to the Manual\n- Chapter 1: Legal Mandate, DRRM Governance and Institutional Accountability\n- Chapter 2: CDRRMO Organizational Structure, Staffing and Human Resource Management\n- Chapter 6: DRRM Financing, Resource Management and Accountability\n- Chapter 8: Stakeholder Engagement and Institutional Partnerships\n\n## Sections merged into this area\n\nThese sections of the earlier two-manual outline were merged here in v1.6. Their codes still find this page.\n\n- EOC Ch.1 (Legal Basis)\n\n## Requirements this area must meet (36 indicators)\n\n- **A1.1** (M, weight 3) City ordinance/EO creating the CDRRMO as a regular office (not ad hoc), with defined functions mirroring RA 10121 Sec. 12(c)  \n  *Basis:* RA 10121 Sec. 12; IRR Rule 6; JMC 2014-1\n- **A1.2** (M, weight 2) CDRRMC constituted with complete membership per RA 10121 Sec. 11 (incl. CSO and private sector reps)  \n  *Basis:* RA 10121 Sec. 11\n- **A1.3** (M, weight 2) CDRRMC meets at least quarterly (and as needed); minutes and resolutions on file  \n  *Basis:* RA 10121 Sec. 11; GKS/SGLG functionality criteria\n- **A1.4** (M, weight 1) CDRRMO serves as CDRRMC secretariat with documented secretariat procedures  \n  *Basis:* RA 10121 Sec. 12(c)(17)\n- **A1.5** (GP, weight 2) Local DRRM-related ordinances in force (e.g., pre-emptive/forced evacuation, no-build zones, hazard-based zoning)  \n  *Basis:* RA 10121 Sec. 12(c)(19); RA 7160; CLUP/ZO\n- **A1.6** (M, weight 3) Protocol for declaring a State of Calamity, incl. CDRRMC recommendation steps and post-declaration measures (State of Imminent Disaster now assessed separately under A1.8)  \n  *Basis:* RA 10121 Sec. 16\n- **A1.7** (GP, weight 1) DRRM is represented in City Development Council and Local Finance Committee deliberations  \n  *Basis:* RA 7160; JMC 2013-1\n- **A1.8** (M, weight 3) State of Imminent Disaster procedure: CDRRMC coordinates with RDRRMC VIII when the pre-disaster risk assessment shows reasonable certainty of severe impact; request format to RDRRMC (24-hour reply); Mayor''s EO template; adoption rule when the Region (or Province, applicability to an ICC to be confirmed) is declared; lifting grounds and authority  \n  *Basis:* RA 12287; RA 12287 IRR (2026) Rule II Sec. 6; Rule III Secs. 2-4\n- **A2.1** (M, weight 3) Organizational structure follows JMC 2014-1: Head + Administration & Training, Research & Planning, and Operations & Warning divisions  \n  *Basis:* NDRRMC-DILG-DBM-CSC JMC 2014-1\n- **A2.2** (M, weight 3) CDRRMO Head is a permanent plantilla position filled by a qualified appointee  \n  *Basis:* RA 10121 Sec. 12(b); JMC 2014-1\n- **A2.3** (M, weight 3) Minimum plantilla positions per JMC 2014-1 created and filled (ratio of filled/required)  \n  *Basis:* JMC 2014-1; CSC QS\n- **A2.4** (M, weight 2) Job descriptions/position descriptions defined for every position, aligned to RA 10121 functions  \n  *Basis:* CSC rules; JMC 2014-1\n- **A2.5** (M, weight 3) 24/7 operations capability with documented shift roster (Operations Center/Duty officers)  \n  *Basis:* RA 10121 Sec. 12(c)(16); EOC guidelines\n- **A2.6** (GP, weight 2) Training needs analysis done and competency-based training plan for staff (ICS, BLS/SFA, WASAR, CSSR, MOSAR, EOC, PDNA, GIS)  \n  *Basis:* RA 10121 Sec. 14; OCD/DRRM Training Institute curricula\n- **A2.7** (M, weight 2) Personnel welfare and safety: insurance, hazard pay, PPE, psychosocial support for responders  \n  *Basis:* RA 10121 Sec. 12; RA 11036 (MHPSS); CSC rules\n- **A2.8** (GP, weight 1) Volunteer/auxiliary responder management system (accreditation, registry, deployment, insurance), incl. mobilization of ACDVs for anticipatory action  \n  *Basis:* RA 10121 Sec. 13; NDRRMC volunteer guidelines; RA 12287 IRR (2026) Rule IV Sec. 5\n- **A2.9** (M, weight 2) Anticipatory action focal person designated in the CDRRMO, with AA training for staff, BDRRMCs, ACDVs and partner CSOs (incl. community-based early warning and early action)  \n  *Basis:* RA 12287 IRR (2026) Rule IV Sec. 1; Rule VII\n- **A2.10** (GP, weight 1) Inventory of DRRM-relevant skills across the CDRRMO, partner offices and barangays (SAR, engineering, logistics, GIS, PDNA, MHPSS) updated within the last 12 months  \n  *Basis:* UNDRR DRSC 6.1.1\n- **A4.1** (M, weight 3) LDRRMF set at not less than 5% of estimated revenue from regular sources  \n  *Basis:* RA 10121 Sec. 21; JMC 2013-1\n- **A4.2** (M, weight 3) 70% Mitigation/Preparedness and 30% Quick Response Fund (QRF) allocation observed  \n  *Basis:* RA 10121 Sec. 21; JMC 2013-1\n- **A4.3** (M, weight 2) Unexpended LDRRMF transferred to Special Trust Fund and used within 5 years  \n  *Basis:* RA 10121 Sec. 21; COA Circular 2012-002\n- **A4.4** (GP, weight 2) LDRRMF utilization rate monitored and reported (target >= 80% of current-year 70% fund)  \n  *Basis:* JMC 2013-1; COA AAR findings\n- **A4.5** (M, weight 2) Emergency procurement procedures (negotiated procurement - emergency cases) documented and pre-arranged (framework agreements, pre-qualified suppliers)  \n  *Basis:* RA 12009 (New Government Procurement Act) & IRR\n- **A4.6** (M, weight 2) Anticipatory action funding pathway: LDRRMFIP sets an AA line within the cap of 10% of the 70% LDRRMF; other sources mapped (Special Trust Fund balances, donations, ODA); Budget, Accounting and BAC procedures allow immediate disbursement and observe the 30%/70% tranche rule around the 3-day lead time  \n  *Basis:* RA 12287; RA 12287 IRR (2026) Rule V Secs. 1-3; RA 10121 Sec. 21; RA 12009\n- **A4.7** (GP, weight 1) Risk transfer/financing instruments explored (indemnity insurance of public assets, PSF access, partnerships)  \n  *Basis:* NDRRMP; RA 10174 (People''s Survival Fund); DOF-BTr NIP\n- **A4.8** (M, weight 2) Clean COA findings on LDRRMF in last audit year (or findings addressed)  \n  *Basis:* COA Circular 2012-002\n- **A4.9** (GP, weight 2) QRF and LDRRMF adequacy tested against the most severe credible scenario (e.g., a Thelma-type flash flood or Yolanda-strength typhoon), with the shortfall and other fund sources identified  \n  *Basis:* UNDRR DRSC 3.2.3, 3.2.4; JMC 2013-1\n- **A10.1** (GP, weight 2) MOAs/ mutual aid agreements with neighbouring LGUs (Kananga, Albuera, Merida, Isabel etc.) and Province of Leyte  \n  *Basis:* RA 10121 Sec. 12(c)(15); RA 7160 Sec. 33\n- **A10.2** (GP, weight 1) Partnerships with CSOs, private sector (incl. energy/geothermal operators), academe and faith-based groups documented, with pre- and post-event roles defined and at least annual coordination meetings  \n  *Basis:* RA 10121 Sec. 12(c)(15); UNDRR DRSC 6.1.2, 6.1.4\n- **A10.3** (M, weight 2) Regular reporting to OCD Region VIII/RDRRMC and DILG (SitReps, LDRRMF reports, Operation L!sto)  \n  *Basis:* RA 10121; DILG MCs\n- **A10.4** (M, weight 2) Monitoring & evaluation framework for LDRRMP with indicators and annual review  \n  *Basis:* RA 10121 Sec. 12(c)(6)\n- **A10.5** (M, weight 1) Full Disclosure Policy: LDRRMF and utilization posted publicly  \n  *Basis:* DILG FDP MCs; RA 10121 Sec. 21\n- **A10.6** (GP, weight 2) After-action reviews conducted after significant events and lessons integrated into plans  \n  *Basis:* NDRRMC; good practice\n- **A10.7** (GP, weight 1) Participation in performance recognition/assessment systems (Gawad KALASAG Seal, SGLG Disaster Preparedness) and gaps acted upon  \n  *Basis:* NDRRMC GKS guidelines; RA 11292 (SGLG Act)\n- **A10.8** (M, weight 2) Post-declaration report within 45 days of lifting a State of Imminent Disaster (declaration status, AA fund utilization, estimated economic and social costs minimized); reporting route confirmed with OCD VIII  \n  *Basis:* RA 12287 IRR (2026) Rule VI Sec. 1\n- **A10.9** (GP, weight 1) Structured learning from other LGUs and networks (exchanges, OCD forums, MCR2030), with resulting changes documented  \n  *Basis:* UNDRR DRSC 6.6.1','Generated from the Inception Report (Annex A) and Traceability v1.1','draft'),
('6a6c34b1-4cae-5af0-90d1-519e425cc2a2'::uuid,'7e47fce7-773f-573e-931b-9df22de0390b'::uuid,'v0.1 outline',E'# Area 3. Preparedness, Planning & Capacity Development\n\n**Part 2: SOPs by alert level**\n\n> Outline generated from the Inception Report (Annex A) and the Traceability Dictionary v1.1. Drafted chapters that serve this area are listed below; write the remaining procedures here or in a new chapter.\n\n## Scope\n\nEmergency plans; contingency plans; SOPs; preparedness standards; training; drills; simulations; competency requirements; EOC readiness; BDRRMC capacity; mutual-aid arrangements.\n\n## MCR2030 alignment\n\n- Primary: Essential 6 – Strengthen Institutional Capacity for Resilience\n- Supporting: Essentials 1, 7, 9\n\n## Drafted chapters for this area\n\n- Chapter 2: CDRRMO Organizational Structure, Staffing and Human Resource Management\n- Chapter 3: Risk Intelligence, DRRM and Contingency Planning, and Institutional Preparedness\n- Chapter 7: Monitoring, Evaluation, Knowledge Management and Continuous Improvement\n- Chapter 8: Stakeholder Engagement and Institutional Partnerships\n\n## Sections merged into this area\n\nThese sections of the earlier two-manual outline were merged here in v1.6. Their codes still find this page.\n\n- EOC Ch.8 (Training and Exercises)\n\n## Requirements this area must meet (17 indicators)\n\n- **A3.1** (M, weight 3) Local DRRM Plan (LDRRMP) current, approved by Sanggunian, aligned with NDRRMP 2020-2030 and Sendai Framework  \n  *Basis:* RA 10121 Sec. 12(c)(6); NDRRMP 2020-2030\n- **A3.2** (M, weight 2) DRR-CCA mainstreamed in CDP, CLUP, ELA and LCCAP (hazard data used in land use and investment decisions)  \n  *Basis:* RA 10121 Sec. 2; RA 9729 as amended by RA 10174; HLURB/DHSUD CLUP guidelines\n- **A3.3** (M, weight 3) Hazard-specific Contingency Plans for priority hazards (flood/flash flood, landslide, earthquake/tsunami, tropical cyclone, industrial/geothermal), updated and tested  \n  *Basis:* NDRRMC CP guidelines; OCD CP Manual\n- **A3.4** (M, weight 2) Public Service Continuity Plan (PSCP) prepared covering CDRRMO and essential city services  \n  *Basis:* NDRRMC/OCD PSCP Guidebook\n- **A3.5** (M, weight 3) Annual LDRRMF Investment Plan (LDRRMFIP) prepared, approved and consistent with LDRRMP  \n  *Basis:* JMC 2013-1\n- **A3.6** (M, weight 3) Evacuation plan with mapped routes, safe zones, centers and pre-emptive evacuation triggers per barangay  \n  *Basis:* RA 10121; RA 12076; DILG Operation L!sto\n- **A3.7** (GP, weight 2) Barangay DRRM plans (85 barangays) reviewed/consolidated by CDRRMO  \n  *Basis:* RA 10121 Sec. 12(c)(6); DILG MC on BDRRM\n- **A7.1** (M, weight 2) Annual training program for city personnel, BDRRMCs, schools and communities implemented  \n  *Basis:* RA 10121 Sec. 12(c)(12), Sec. 14\n- **A7.2** (M, weight 2) Participation in quarterly Nationwide Simultaneous Earthquake Drill (NSED) and hazard-specific drills with evaluation  \n  *Basis:* NDRRMC NSED guidelines\n- **A7.3** (GP, weight 2) BDRRMC functionality across 85 barangays assessed (e.g., Listo si KAP) with support plan for low-functioning barangays  \n  *Basis:* RA 10121; DILG MC 2025-035 (Listo si KAP)\n- **A7.4** (M, weight 3) Permanent evacuation center(s) planned/established and existing ECs meet minimum standards (WASH, privacy, PWD access, child-friendly space)  \n  *Basis:* RA 12076 (Ligtas Pinoy Centers Act); RA 10821; DSWD standards\n- **A7.5** (M, weight 2) Prepositioned relief stocks/food packs and non-food items with inventory and replenishment triggers  \n  *Basis:* RA 10121; DSWD-LGU protocols; Operation L!sto\n- **A7.6** (M, weight 2) Inclusive DRRM: GAD, PWD, senior citizen, children, IP considerations embedded in plans and services, with vulnerable-sector representatives confirming they were engaged  \n  *Basis:* RA 9710; RA 7277 as amended; RA 9994; RA 10821; RA 8371; RA 12287 IRR (2026) Rule IV Sec. 1(a); UNDRR DRSC 7.2.2\n- **A7.7** (GP, weight 1) Schools, hospitals and critical facilities included in preparedness planning and drills  \n  *Basis:* DepEd/DOH DRRM policies; Safe Schools/Hospitals\n- **A7.8** (GP, weight 1) Refresher cycle (at least annual) set for trained responders, EOC staff and BDRRMC members, with attendance tracked  \n  *Basis:* UNDRR DRSC 6.4.2\n- **A7.9** (GP, weight 2) BDRRMCs can account for residents of affected puroks within 12 hours of impact (welfare check), shown in a drill or a real event  \n  *Basis:* UNDRR DRSC 7.2.1\n- **C5.1** (GP, weight 1) Business continuity outreach to local businesses based on shared hazard scenarios (outreach only; no mandate implied)  \n  *Basis:* UNDRR DRSC 7.3.2','Generated from the Inception Report (Annex A) and Traceability v1.1','draft'),
('364be216-bbc8-5cf4-b50d-207e569e75b4'::uuid,'69e884bf-8590-5061-99a1-38fb8c0769a4'::uuid,'v0.1 outline',E'# Area 4. EOC Activation, Incident Management & Coordination\n\n**Part 2: SOPs by alert level**\n\n> Outline generated from the Inception Report (Annex A) and the Traceability Dictionary v1.1. Drafted chapters that serve this area are listed below; write the remaining procedures here or in a new chapter.\n\n## Scope\n\nAlert levels; activation/deactivation; ICS integration; incident objectives; command and coordination; operational periods; EOC staffing; escalation; transition from response to recovery.\n\n## MCR2030 alignment\n\n- Primary: Essential 9 – Ensure Effective Disaster Response\n- Supporting: Essentials 1, 6, 10\n\n## Drafted chapters for this area\n\n- Chapter 4: Early Warning, EOC Activation, Incident Management and Emergency Response\n\n## Sections merged into this area\n\nThese sections of the earlier two-manual outline were merged here in v1.6. Their codes still find this page.\n\n- EOC Ch.2 (Concept of Operations and Activation)\n- EOC Ch.5 (Organization, Staffing and Public Information)\n\n## Requirements this area must meet (24 indicators)\n\n- **A8.1** (M, weight 3) Incident Command System institutionalized: EO on ICS, trained IMT roster, pre-designated Incident Commanders  \n  *Basis:* NDRRMC MC No. 4, s. 2012 (ICS)\n- **A8.2** (M, weight 3) Organized and trained response teams: SAR (WASAR/CSSR/HAZMAT as relevant), EMS/ambulance, fire coordination with BFP  \n  *Basis:* RA 10121 Sec. 12(c)(16); RA 11589 (BFP)\n- **A8.3** (M, weight 2) Response equipment and vehicles inventoried, serviceable and maintained (preventive maintenance schedule)  \n  *Basis:* COA property rules; RA 10121\n- **A8.4** (GP, weight 2) Emergency hotline integrated with E911 and dispatch protocol (call-taking to dispatch time tracked)  \n  *Basis:* EO 56 s. 2018 (E911); DILG guidelines\n- **A8.5** (M, weight 2) Response clusters organized at city level mirroring national cluster approach (Food & NFI, Health, WASH, CCCM, Logistics, Search Rescue & Retrieval, Law & Order, Education, Protection, ETC, MDM)  \n  *Basis:* NDCC MC No. 12, s. 2008; NDRRM Plan Response pillar\n- **A8.6** (M, weight 3) Pre-Disaster Risk Assessment (PDRA) conducted before forecast hazards, with anticipatory actions recorded  \n  *Basis:* NDRRMC PDRA protocol; RA 12287; RA 12287 IRR (2026) Rule II Sec. 5\n- **A8.7** (M, weight 2) Management of the Dead and Missing (MDM) and Rapid Damage Assessment & Needs Analysis (RDANA) teams designated and trained  \n  *Basis:* NDRRMC MDM & RDANA guidelines\n- **A8.8** (M, weight 3) Anticipatory action protocols by hazard and lead time: office-order templates for prepositioning (relief, medical supplies, animal feed, water and power for evacuation centers), deployment of heavy equipment, transport and personnel, pre-emptive evacuation incl. livestock and pets, CCCM, and safeguarding of critical infrastructure; aligned with CPs, Oplan L!sto and evacuation plans  \n  *Basis:* RA 12287 IRR (2026) Rule IV Secs. 1, 3, 4, 6\n- **A8.9** (M, weight 2) Anticipatory social amelioration: families identified and prioritized using CBMS or the prevailing registry; data-sharing agreements compliant with RA 10173; local guidelines for anticipatory cash or vouchers issued with the CSWDO  \n  *Basis:* RA 12287 IRR (2026) Rule IV Sec. 7; RA 11315 (CBMS); RA 10173\n- **B1.1** (M, weight 3) EOC established by EO/ordinance with defined mandate, authority and relationship to CDRRMC and ICS  \n  *Basis:* NDRRMC Memorandum No. 131, s. 2018 (EOC Guidelines); RA 10121\n- **B1.2** (M, weight 3) Alert/activation levels defined (e.g., White-normal, Blue-alert, Red-full activation) with hazard-based triggers and a defined EOC posture when a State of Imminent Disaster is declared  \n  *Basis:* National Disaster Response Plan; RDRRMC VIII Res. No. 12-006, s. 2023; NDRRMC Memorandum No. 131, s. 2018; RA 12287 IRR (2026) Rule IV Sec. 1\n- **B1.3** (M, weight 3) Activation, escalation, de-escalation and deactivation procedures with designated authority  \n  *Basis:* NDRRMC EOC Guidelines\n- **B1.4** (M, weight 2) Concept of operations documents EOC functions: coordination, information management, resource management, policy support  \n  *Basis:* NDRRMC EOC Guidelines\n- **B1.5** (M, weight 2) EOC linkage to Provincial (Leyte) and Regional (OCD VIII) EOCs defined  \n  *Basis:* NDRRMC EOC Guidelines\n- **B4.1** (M, weight 3) EOC organizational structure defined (EOC Manager, Operations, Planning/Information, Logistics, Admin/Finance, liaison desks)  \n  *Basis:* NDRRMC EOC Guidelines; ICS\n- **B4.2** (M, weight 3) Pre-designated EOC staff with alternates (at least 2 deep per key position)  \n  *Basis:* NDRRMC EOC Guidelines\n- **B4.3** (M, weight 2) Duty roster for sustained 24/7 operations with shift handover protocol  \n  *Basis:* Good practice\n- **B4.4** (M, weight 2) Agency/cluster liaison desks identified (CSWDO, CHO, CEO, PNP, BFP, AFP, DepEd, utilities, Red Cross)  \n  *Basis:* NDCC MC 12 s. 2008; EOC Guidelines\n- **B4.5** (GP, weight 2) Position checklists/job action sheets for each EOC role  \n  *Basis:* Good practice\n- **B4.6** (GP, weight 1) Responder welfare in EOC: rest cycles, meals, MHPSS, family support  \n  *Basis:* RA 11036; good practice\n- **C4.1** (GP, weight 3) Health anticipatory action: Health Cluster activation, facility service-continuity and surge plans, prepositioned commodities, health emergency response teams on standby  \n  *Basis:* RA 12287 IRR (2026) Rule IV Sec. 9\n- **C4.2** (GP, weight 2) Education anticipatory action: schools'' AA plans and learning-continuity modalities  \n  *Basis:* RA 12287 IRR (2026) Rule IV Sec. 10(a); RA 10821\n- **C4.3** (GP, weight 2) Agri-fisheries anticipatory action using RSBSA, FishR and livestock registries; early action guidelines on storage, inputs and animal health  \n  *Basis:* RA 12287 IRR (2026) Rule IV Sec. 8\n- **C4.4** (GP, weight 1) Pre-impact price monitoring and anti-profiteering of basic goods  \n  *Basis:* RA 12287 IRR (2026) Rule IV Sec. 10(c); RA 7581 (Price Act)','Generated from the Inception Report (Annex A) and Traceability v1.1','draft'),
('56a3017d-d58a-5530-9aad-45a8dda26d35'::uuid,'5536a613-b08a-5c03-b7d3-387341294c0b'::uuid,'v0.1 outline',E'# Area 7. Resource, Logistics & Emergency Support Management\n\n**Part 2: SOPs by alert level**\n\n> Outline generated from the Inception Report (Annex A) and the Traceability Dictionary v1.1. Drafted chapters that serve this area are listed below; write the remaining procedures here or in a new chapter.\n\n## Scope\n\nResource inventory; resource requests; procurement; stockpiling; staging; transport; warehousing; fuel; relief supplies; mutual aid; supplier networks; emergency support services.\n\n## MCR2030 alignment\n\n- Primary: Essential 9 – Ensure Effective Disaster Response\n- Supporting: Essentials 3, 8, 6\n\n## Drafted chapters for this area\n\n- Chapter 6: DRRM Financing, Resource Management and Accountability\n- Chapter 8: Stakeholder Engagement and Institutional Partnerships\n\n## Sections merged into this area\n\nThese sections of the earlier two-manual outline were merged here in v1.6. Their codes still find this page.\n\n- EOC Ch.7 (Coordination and Resource Management)\n\n## Requirements this area must meet (6 indicators)\n\n- **B6.1** (M, weight 3) ICS-EOC interface defined: EOC supports Incident Commander(s); no duplication of command  \n  *Basis:* NDRRMC MC No. 4 s. 2012; EOC Guidelines\n- **B6.2** (M, weight 3) Resource management system: request, tracking, mobilization and demobilization of resources  \n  *Basis:* ICS resource management; EOC Guidelines\n- **B6.3** (M, weight 2) Resource inventory (city, barangays, partners, private sector) accessible from EOC  \n  *Basis:* RA 10121; ICS\n- **B6.4** (GP, weight 1) Procedures for receiving and managing external assistance/ donations and volunteers  \n  *Basis:* NDRRMC guidelines on international/ external assistance\n- **B6.5** (GP, weight 2) Decision-support briefings to CDRRMC/Mayor at fixed intervals during activation  \n  *Basis:* EOC Guidelines\n- **B6.6** (GP, weight 2) Pre-arranged resource commitments from partners and suppliers set out by item, quantity, activation trigger and contact in signed agreements (incl. supplier agreements tapped for anticipatory action)  \n  *Basis:* UNDRR DRSC 1.2.4; RA 12287 IRR (2026) Rule IV Sec. 6(a)(ii)','Generated from the Inception Report (Annex A) and Traceability v1.1','draft'),
('c0789041-41bf-583e-bc08-d78a8037f0a5'::uuid,'c80fd8d0-da01-59c9-9e9d-5d47c79bd9ed'::uuid,'v0.1 outline',E'# Area 8. Responder Safety, Welfare & Inclusive Emergency Operations\n\n**Part 2: SOPs by alert level**\n\n> Outline generated from the Inception Report (Annex A) and the Traceability Dictionary v1.1. Drafted chapters that serve this area are listed below; write the remaining procedures here or in a new chapter.\n\n## Scope\n\nDuty of care; PPE; responder health and safety; psychosocial support; fatigue management; workforce rotation; gender/inclusion considerations; protection of vulnerable groups; safe operating procedures.\n\n## MCR2030 alignment\n\n- Primary: Essential 9 – Ensure Effective Disaster Response\n- Supporting: Essentials 6, 7, 8\n\n## Drafted chapters for this area\n\n- Chapter 2: CDRRMO Organizational Structure, Staffing and Human Resource Management\n\n## Sections merged into this area\n\nThese sections of the earlier two-manual outline were merged here in v1.6. Their codes still find this page.\n\n- None.\n\n## Requirements this area must meet (0 indicators)\n\n- None yet. No indicator in the Traceability Dictionary v1.1 names this as its primary area.','Generated from the Inception Report (Annex A) and Traceability v1.1','draft'),
('db0ebf4f-9b9c-539f-b3e1-26430b7cd27d'::uuid,'20cfcb06-f3b6-545f-9d11-b9aeb93a28d2'::uuid,'v0.1 outline',E'# Area 2. Risk Intelligence, Prevention & Mitigation\n\n**Part 3: Information management and public communication**\n\n> Outline generated from the Inception Report (Annex A) and the Traceability Dictionary v1.1. Drafted chapters that serve this area are listed below; write the remaining procedures here or in a new chapter.\n\n## Scope\n\nMulti-hazard risk assessment; hazard/exposure/vulnerability analysis; climate risk; risk scenarios; GIS-based risk information; prevention and mitigation measures; risk-informed development planning.\n\n## MCR2030 alignment\n\n- Primary: Essential 2 – Identify, Understand and Use Current and Future Risk Scenarios\n- Supporting: Essentials 4, 5, 8\n\n## Drafted chapters for this area\n\n- Chapter 3: Risk Intelligence, DRRM and Contingency Planning, and Institutional Preparedness\n\n## Sections merged into this area\n\nThese sections of the earlier two-manual outline were merged here in v1.6. Their codes still find this page.\n\n- None.\n\n## Requirements this area must meet (19 indicators)\n\n- **A5.1** (M, weight 3) Updated hazard maps for all priority hazards (MGB, PHIVOLCS, PAGASA, GeoRiskPH/HazardHunterPH) at barangay scale  \n  *Basis:* RA 10121 Sec. 12(c)(3); NDRRMP\n- **A5.2** (M, weight 3) Climate & Disaster Risk Assessment (CDRA)/ CRA completed with exposure (population, buildings, critical facilities) and vulnerability data  \n  *Basis:* DHSUD/CCC CDRA guidelines; RA 10121 Sec. 12(c)(3)\n- **A5.3** (M, weight 2) Disaggregated population database (sex, age, disability, IP, pregnant/lactating) for at-risk households  \n  *Basis:* RA 10121 Sec. 12(c)(5); RA 9710; RA 7277 as amended; RA 10821\n- **A5.4** (GP, weight 2) DRRM information system/ database with disaster event history, damage and losses (incl. 1991 flood, 2013 Yolanda, 2017 earthquake records)  \n  *Basis:* RA 10121 Sec. 12(c)(5); Sendai monitoring\n- **A5.5** (M, weight 2) Data privacy compliance for beneficiary and affected-population data (DPO, consent, data sharing agreements)  \n  *Basis:* RA 10173 (Data Privacy Act); NPC circulars\n- **A5.6** (GP, weight 1) GIS capability (software, trained staff, updated base maps) within Research & Planning  \n  *Basis:* JMC 2014-1 (R&P functions)\n- **A5.7** (GP, weight 2) One maintained, shared source of risk and readiness information (hazard maps, plans, contacts, readiness summary) open to CDRRMC member offices, with a public summary posted  \n  *Basis:* UNDRR DRSC 1.4.1, 6.3.1, 6.3.2; RA 10173\n- **A5.8** (GP, weight 2) Critical facilities list (EOC, hospitals, evacuation centers, water, power, telecom, bridges, port) with dependencies mapped as potential failure chains and used to set protection and restoration priorities  \n  *Basis:* UNDRR DRSC 2.3.1; RA 12287 IRR (2026) Rule I Sec. 5(b),(d)\n- **A5.9** (GP, weight 1) Agreed update cycle: hazard data every 3 years or less; exposure, vulnerability and critical-facility data every 18 months or less  \n  *Basis:* UNDRR DRSC 2.5.1\n- **C1.1** (GP, weight 2) Most-probable and most-severe risk scenarios inform CDP/CLUP priorities and the location of major investments  \n  *Basis:* UNDRR DRSC 1.1.1; RA 10121 Sec. 2; DHSUD CLUP guidelines\n- **C1.2** (GP, weight 1) DRR/CCA screening step in project and budget approval (LDC, LFC)  \n  *Basis:* UNDRR DRSC 1.3.1; climate change expenditure tagging guidelines\n- **C1.3** (GP, weight 1) CDRA estimates losses beyond physical assets: livelihoods and jobs, housing and displacement, agriculture, ecosystems, cultural heritage  \n  *Basis:* UNDRR DRSC 2.2.2; DHSUD/CCC CDRA guidelines\n- **C1.4** (GP, weight 2) Risk-sensitive development guidelines applied in zoning and building permits, based on hazard maps  \n  *Basis:* UNDRR DRSC 2.4.1; CLUP/ZO\n- **C2.1** (GP, weight 3) Structural safety of the EOC, evacuation centers and critical public facilities assessed by the Building Official, with a rapid safety inspection procedure before forecast impact  \n  *Basis:* UNDRR DRSC 4.3.1, 4.4.2; PD 1096; RA 12076; RA 12287 IRR (2026) Rule IV Sec. 4(c)(i)\n- **C2.2** (GP, weight 2) Pre-crisis and priority-restoration arrangements with power, water and telecom providers (load-shedding and water-rationing plans, cell-on-wheels, restoration priority list)  \n  *Basis:* UNDRR DRSC Essential 8; RA 12287 IRR (2026) Rule IV Sec. 4(c)(ii)-(iv)\n- **C2.3** (GP, weight 2) Transport anticipatory actions: pre-inspection of bridges, alternate routes and traffic teams, coordination with seaport and terminal operators  \n  *Basis:* UNDRR DRSC Essential 8; RA 12287 IRR (2026) Rule IV Sec. 10(b)\n- **C3.1** (GP, weight 2) Critical protective ecosystems (upper Anilao-Malbasag watershed, upland forest cover, coastal mangroves) identified and monitored as risk-reduction assets  \n  *Basis:* UNDRR DRSC 5.1.1; RA 9729 as amended\n- **C3.2** (GP, weight 1) Arrangements with neighbouring LGUs and DENR where watersheds or protective ecosystems extend beyond city limits  \n  *Basis:* UNDRR DRSC 5.3.1, 5.3.2; RA 7160 Sec. 33\n- **C3.3** (GP, weight 2) Environmental anticipatory actions: declogging of waterways and drainage, slope stabilization, safe debris and carcass disposal  \n  *Basis:* RA 12287 IRR (2026) Rule IV Sec. 10(d)','Generated from the Inception Report (Annex A) and Traceability v1.1','draft'),
('ae115587-bd0c-5f5b-ae64-eeaee4b23bff'::uuid,'8f0b8bd9-10dc-54b5-9032-cb131ce251b6'::uuid,'v0.1 outline',E'# Area 5. Early Warning, Emergency Communications & Public Information\n\n**Part 3: Information management and public communication**\n\n> Outline generated from the Inception Report (Annex A) and the Traceability Dictionary v1.1. Drafted chapters that serve this area are listed below; write the remaining procedures here or in a new chapter.\n\n## Scope\n\nMonitoring; detection; warning thresholds; multi-channel dissemination; public information; risk communication; accessible alerts; community feedback; rumor management; warning verification.\n\n## MCR2030 alignment\n\n- Primary: Essential 9 – Ensure Effective Disaster Response\n- Supporting: Essentials 2, 7, 6\n\n## Drafted chapters for this area\n\n- Chapter 4: Early Warning, EOC Activation, Incident Management and Emergency Response\n\n## Sections merged into this area\n\nThese sections of the earlier two-manual outline were merged here in v1.6. Their codes still find this page.\n\n- EOC Ch.4 (Communications and Sector Coordination)\n\n## Requirements this area must meet (7 indicators)\n\n- **A6.1** (M, weight 3) Hazard-specific EWS operational for flood (incl. Anilao/Malbasag river systems), rain-induced landslide, tsunami (Ormoc Bay) and tropical cyclone  \n  *Basis:* RA 10121 Sec. 12(c)(8); PAGASA/PHIVOLCS protocols\n- **A6.2** (M, weight 3) Warning thresholds linked to specific actions (alert levels -> pre-emptive evacuation, class/work suspension, State of Imminent Disaster request) in written protocols, built to take up NDRRMC impact-based triggers once issued  \n  *Basis:* RA 10121; RA 12287; RA 12287 IRR (2026) Rule II Sec. 2; DILG Operation L!sto\n- **A6.3** (M, weight 3) Last-mile dissemination channels tested to barangay/purok level (sirens, radio, SMS/ECBS, social media, barangay criers)  \n  *Basis:* RA 10639 (Free Mobile Disaster Alerts); NDRRMC EWS\n- **A6.4** (GP, weight 2) Warnings issued in local language (Cebuano/ Ormocanon) and accessible formats (sign language, visual alerts for PWD)  \n  *Basis:* RA 10121; RA 11106 (FSL Act); RA 7277\n- **A6.5** (GP, weight 1) Designated public information officer and risk communication plan (incl. rumor/misinformation management)  \n  *Basis:* NDRRMC public info protocols\n- **A6.6** (GP, weight 1) IEC program on hazards and preparedness with annual reach targets  \n  *Basis:* RA 10121 Sec. 12(c)(13)\n- **A6.7** (M, weight 2) Templates and channels for public notice of a State of Imminent Disaster and of the anticipatory actions required, incl. sector-specific impact-based advisories and reach to geographically isolated barangays  \n  *Basis:* RA 12287 IRR (2026) Rule IV Sec. 2','Generated from the Inception Report (Annex A) and Traceability v1.1','draft'),
('2a4cf582-f0e0-5270-9983-c99cf748825a'::uuid,'c4693fb2-e773-5bae-ad3a-be15c30b6131'::uuid,'v0.1 outline',E'# Area 6. Situational Awareness, Information Management & GIS\n\n**Part 3: Information management and public communication**\n\n> Outline generated from the Inception Report (Annex A) and the Traceability Dictionary v1.1. Drafted chapters that serve this area are listed below; write the remaining procedures here or in a new chapter.\n\n## Scope\n\nData collection; validation; common operating picture; GIS; dashboards; incident reports; SITREPs; data standards; information-sharing; decision support; risk intelligence.\n\n## MCR2030 alignment\n\n- Primary: Essential 2 – Identify, Understand and Use Current and Future Risk Scenarios\n- Supporting: Essentials 6, 9, 8\n\n## Drafted chapters for this area\n\n- None yet.\n\n## Sections merged into this area\n\nThese sections of the earlier two-manual outline were merged here in v1.6. Their codes still find this page.\n\n- EOC Ch.6 (Information Management and Reporting)\n\n## Requirements this area must meet (7 indicators)\n\n- **B5.1** (M, weight 3) Standard SitRep/ Report templates aligned with NDRRMC/OCD formats and fixed reporting schedule  \n  *Basis:* NDRRMC reporting protocol\n- **B5.2** (M, weight 3) Barangay-to-city reporting flow (BDRRMC -> EOC) with defined timelines and formats  \n  *Basis:* RA 10121; DILG\n- **B5.3** (GP, weight 2) Common Operating Picture maintained (dashboard/ GIS map of incidents, evacuees, resources)  \n  *Basis:* NDRRMC EOC Guidelines\n- **B5.4** (M, weight 2) Evacuation center and affected-family tracking (DAFAC/ registration) feeds EOC data  \n  *Basis:* DSWD DAFAC; RA 10821\n- **B5.5** (M, weight 2) EOC logbook/ significant events log and document retention  \n  *Basis:* Good practice; NAP rules\n- **B5.6** (M, weight 2) Weather/hazard monitoring routine (PAGASA, PHIVOLCS feeds) with bulletins logged and disseminated  \n  *Basis:* RA 10121; PAGASA protocols\n- **B5.7** (GP, weight 1) Inbound citizen reporting (hotline, SMS, social media) feeds the common operating picture after a verification step  \n  *Basis:* UNDRR DRSC 7.4.2','Generated from the Inception Report (Annex A) and Traceability v1.1','draft'),
('afdf02a8-6b39-55d8-ba27-24c5a1da45f3'::uuid,'f6c14690-1c4d-5022-95b7-04dc0e2e0c01'::uuid,'v0.1 outline',E'# Area 9. Digital Continuity, Cybersecurity & Systems Resilience\n\n**Part 4: Continuity and infrastructure safeguards**\n\n> Outline generated from the Inception Report (Annex A) and the Traceability Dictionary v1.1. Drafted chapters that serve this area are listed below; write the remaining procedures here or in a new chapter.\n\n## Scope\n\nCritical information systems; cybersecurity; data protection; backups; cloud redundancy; alternate communications; power continuity; disaster recovery; system interoperability; continuity of operations.\n\n## MCR2030 alignment\n\n- Primary: Essential 8 – Increase Infrastructure Resilience\n- Supporting: Essentials 6, 9, 4\n\n## Drafted chapters for this area\n\n- None yet.\n\n## Sections merged into this area\n\nThese sections of the earlier two-manual outline were merged here in v1.6. Their codes still find this page.\n\n- EOC Ch.3 (Facility, Site and Continuity)\n\n## Requirements this area must meet (13 indicators)\n\n- **B2.1** (M, weight 3) EOC site located outside high flood, landslide, tsunami and liquefaction zones (checked vs hazard maps)  \n  *Basis:* NDRRMC EOC Guidelines; hazard maps\n- **B2.2** (M, weight 3) Building structural integrity assessed (seismic - Philippine Fault proximity) and certified  \n  *Basis:* NBC (PD 1096); NSCP; DPWH\n- **B2.3** (M, weight 3) Backup power (generator + fuel for >=72 hours, UPS) tested regularly  \n  *Basis:* NDRRMC EOC Guidelines; good practice\n- **B2.4** (GP, weight 2) Functional layout: operations floor, briefing/decision room, comms room, rest area, sanitation, kitchen  \n  *Basis:* NDRRMC EOC Guidelines\n- **B2.5** (GP, weight 1) Water, food and sanitation supplies for EOC staff for >=72 hours  \n  *Basis:* Good practice; PSCP\n- **B2.6** (GP, weight 1) Physical security and access control (ID, visitor log, CCTV)  \n  *Basis:* Good practice\n- **B2.7** (M, weight 2) Designated and equipped alternate EOC with relocation procedure  \n  *Basis:* PSCP Guidebook; NDRRMC EOC Guidelines\n- **B3.1** (M, weight 3) Redundant communications: VHF/UHF radio, HF, satellite phone, landline, mobile, internet (min. 3 independent channels)  \n  *Basis:* NDRRMC EOC Guidelines; NTC frequency assignment\n- **B3.2** (M, weight 2) Radio network covering all 85 barangays and responders, with call signs and net-control procedure  \n  *Basis:* NTC licensing; ETC cluster\n- **B3.3** (GP, weight 2) Backup internet (secondary ISP/satellite) and continuity of digital systems  \n  *Basis:* Good practice; DICT\n- **B3.4** (M, weight 2) Communications plan/ directory (agencies, barangays, clusters) updated within last 6 months  \n  *Basis:* NDRRMC EOC Guidelines\n- **B3.5** (GP, weight 1) Cybersecurity and information security measures for EOC systems  \n  *Basis:* RA 10173; DICT National Cybersecurity Plan\n- **B3.6** (GP, weight 1) Display and monitoring equipment (video wall/monitors, weather feeds, CCTV feeds)  \n  *Basis:* Good practice','Generated from the Inception Report (Annex A) and Traceability v1.1','draft'),
('82124c03-efa3-5c75-af8e-452e003f306f'::uuid,'24c36b6b-9a56-5f61-acb4-8a529b7fc33c'::uuid,'v0.1 outline',E'# Area 10. Recovery, Learning, Performance & Continuous Improvement\n\n**Part 5: Recovery and continuous improvement**\n\n> Outline generated from the Inception Report (Annex A) and the Traceability Dictionary v1.1. Drafted chapters that serve this area are listed below; write the remaining procedures here or in a new chapter.\n\n## Scope\n\nRecovery transition; damage/loss assessment; debris management; rehabilitation/reconstruction; Build Back Better; economic recovery; AARs; M&E; audits; exercises; lessons learned; manual revision.\n\n## MCR2030 alignment\n\n- Primary: Essential 10 – Expedite Recovery and Build Back Better\n- Supporting: Essentials 3, 6, 7, 8, 9\n\n## Drafted chapters for this area\n\n- Chapter 5: Recovery, Rehabilitation and Build Back Better\n- Chapter 7: Monitoring, Evaluation, Knowledge Management and Continuous Improvement\n\n## Sections merged into this area\n\nThese sections of the earlier two-manual outline were merged here in v1.6. Their codes still find this page.\n\n- EOC Ch.9 (Sustainability)\n\n## Requirements this area must meet (11 indicators)\n\n- **A9.1** (GP, weight 2) Post-Disaster Needs Assessment (PDNA) capacity: trained team and templates ready  \n  *Basis:* NDRRMC PDNA guidelines; OCD\n- **A9.2** (M, weight 2) Rehabilitation & recovery plan prepared after major events, with build-back-better and resettlement provisions  \n  *Basis:* RA 10121 Sec. 12(c)(11); NDRRMP Pillar 4\n- **A9.3** (GP, weight 1) Recovery data (damage, losses, livelihood, housing) tracked to completion  \n  *Basis:* Sendai Framework targets C-D\n- **A9.4** (GP, weight 1) Psychosocial and livelihood recovery services coordinated with CSWDO, CHO, PESO  \n  *Basis:* RA 11036; DSWD protocols\n- **A9.5** (GP, weight 2) Pre-disaster recovery framework: roles, PDNA activation, temporary shelter, debris management and recovery fund sources agreed before an event  \n  *Basis:* UNDRR DRSC Essential 10; NDRRMP Pillar 4\n- **B7.1** (M, weight 3) Written EOC SOPs/ Manual approved and disseminated to all EOC staff  \n  *Basis:* NDRRMC EOC Guidelines\n- **B7.2** (M, weight 2) EOC staff trained (EOC operations course, ICS, IM) with records  \n  *Basis:* OCD/DRRM training; NDRRMC EOC Guidelines\n- **B7.3** (M, weight 2) Annual exercise program (tabletop, functional, full-scale) testing EOC activation  \n  *Basis:* NDRRMC; HSEEP-style good practice\n- **B7.4** (GP, weight 2) After-action review after each activation with improvement plan tracked  \n  *Basis:* Good practice\n- **B7.5** (M, weight 2) Dedicated EOC budget for operations, maintenance and upgrades in LDRRMFIP  \n  *Basis:* JMC 2013-1\n- **B7.6** (GP, weight 1) Equipment maintenance schedule and annual EOC readiness self-check  \n  *Basis:* Good practice; PSCP','Generated from the Inception Report (Annex A) and Traceability v1.1','draft'),
('e5349593-5716-53d3-a70b-0bc082ee8680'::uuid,'91559d3e-3452-546c-ad4f-8b66c64cd08a'::uuid,'v0.1 skeleton',E'# MOO Ch.0 – Introduction\n\n> Skeleton generated from IAT v1.1. Replace each requirement with the City''s procedure, standard or form.\n\n## Requirements this section must meet\n\n- None yet. No indicator in the Traceability Dictionary v1.1 names this as its primary area.','Generated from IAT v1.1','draft'),
('46712f75-47ec-5a35-932e-6825746f926a'::uuid,'c906fb73-66a3-5477-8732-349b15f6e5c4'::uuid,'v0.1 skeleton',E'# MOO Ch.1 – Legal and Institutional Framework\n\n> Skeleton generated from IAT v1.1. Replace each requirement with the City''s procedure, standard or form.\n\n## Requirements this section must meet\n\n- **A1.1** (M, weight 3) City ordinance/EO creating the CDRRMO as a regular office (not ad hoc), with defined functions mirroring RA 10121 Sec. 12(c)  \n  *Basis:* RA 10121 Sec. 12; IRR Rule 6; JMC 2014-1\n- **A1.2** (M, weight 2) CDRRMC constituted with complete membership per RA 10121 Sec. 11 (incl. CSO and private sector reps)  \n  *Basis:* RA 10121 Sec. 11\n- **A1.3** (M, weight 2) CDRRMC meets at least quarterly (and as needed); minutes and resolutions on file  \n  *Basis:* RA 10121 Sec. 11; GKS/SGLG functionality criteria\n- **A1.5** (GP, weight 2) Local DRRM-related ordinances in force (e.g., pre-emptive/forced evacuation, no-build zones, hazard-based zoning)  \n  *Basis:* RA 10121 Sec. 12(c)(19); RA 7160; CLUP/ZO\n- **A1.6** (M, weight 3) Protocol for declaring a State of Calamity, incl. CDRRMC recommendation steps and post-declaration measures (State of Imminent Disaster now assessed separately under A1.8)  \n  *Basis:* RA 10121 Sec. 16\n- **A1.7** (GP, weight 1) DRRM is represented in City Development Council and Local Finance Committee deliberations  \n  *Basis:* RA 7160; JMC 2013-1\n- **A1.8** (M, weight 3) State of Imminent Disaster procedure: CDRRMC coordinates with RDRRMC VIII when the pre-disaster risk assessment shows reasonable certainty of severe impact; request format to RDRRMC (24-hour reply); Mayor''s EO template; adoption rule when the Region (or Province, applicability to an ICC to be confirmed) is declared; lifting grounds and authority  \n  *Basis:* RA 12287; RA 12287 IRR (2026) Rule II Sec. 6; Rule III Secs. 2-4','Generated from IAT v1.1','draft'),
('3f1cb2eb-5bb2-5c0d-bd0b-dc623233dc05'::uuid,'f379ea8e-ae82-5eb6-9887-f700227215ce'::uuid,'v0.1 skeleton',E'# MOO Ch.2 – Office Organization\n\n> Skeleton generated from IAT v1.1. Replace each requirement with the City''s procedure, standard or form.\n\n## Requirements this section must meet\n\n- **A1.4** (M, weight 1) CDRRMO serves as CDRRMC secretariat with documented secretariat procedures  \n  *Basis:* RA 10121 Sec. 12(c)(17)\n- **A2.1** (M, weight 3) Organizational structure follows JMC 2014-1: Head + Administration & Training, Research & Planning, and Operations & Warning divisions  \n  *Basis:* NDRRMC-DILG-DBM-CSC JMC 2014-1\n- **A2.2** (M, weight 3) CDRRMO Head is a permanent plantilla position filled by a qualified appointee  \n  *Basis:* RA 10121 Sec. 12(b); JMC 2014-1\n- **A2.3** (M, weight 3) Minimum plantilla positions per JMC 2014-1 created and filled (ratio of filled/required)  \n  *Basis:* JMC 2014-1; CSC QS\n- **A2.4** (M, weight 2) Job descriptions/position descriptions defined for every position, aligned to RA 10121 functions  \n  *Basis:* CSC rules; JMC 2014-1\n- **A2.7** (M, weight 2) Personnel welfare and safety: insurance, hazard pay, PPE, psychosocial support for responders  \n  *Basis:* RA 10121 Sec. 12; RA 11036 (MHPSS); CSC rules\n- **A2.9** (M, weight 2) Anticipatory action focal person designated in the CDRRMO, with AA training for staff, BDRRMCs, ACDVs and partner CSOs (incl. community-based early warning and early action)  \n  *Basis:* RA 12287 IRR (2026) Rule IV Sec. 1; Rule VII','Generated from IAT v1.1','draft'),
('5ac43e3f-4099-51cb-b931-a68cfd65256a'::uuid,'77080547-c4e3-52f7-8908-02ce0fc78258'::uuid,'v0.1 skeleton',E'# MOO Ch.3 – DRRM and Contingency Planning\n\n> Skeleton generated from IAT v1.1. Replace each requirement with the City''s procedure, standard or form.\n\n## Requirements this section must meet\n\n- **A2.6** (GP, weight 2) Training needs analysis done and competency-based training plan for staff (ICS, BLS/SFA, WASAR, CSSR, MOSAR, EOC, PDNA, GIS)  \n  *Basis:* RA 10121 Sec. 14; OCD/DRRM Training Institute curricula\n- **A2.8** (GP, weight 1) Volunteer/auxiliary responder management system (accreditation, registry, deployment, insurance), incl. mobilization of ACDVs for anticipatory action  \n  *Basis:* RA 10121 Sec. 13; NDRRMC volunteer guidelines; RA 12287 IRR (2026) Rule IV Sec. 5\n- **A2.9** (M, weight 2) Anticipatory action focal person designated in the CDRRMO, with AA training for staff, BDRRMCs, ACDVs and partner CSOs (incl. community-based early warning and early action)  \n  *Basis:* RA 12287 IRR (2026) Rule IV Sec. 1; Rule VII\n- **A2.10** (GP, weight 1) Inventory of DRRM-relevant skills across the CDRRMO, partner offices and barangays (SAR, engineering, logistics, GIS, PDNA, MHPSS) updated within the last 12 months  \n  *Basis:* UNDRR DRSC 6.1.1\n- **A3.1** (M, weight 3) Local DRRM Plan (LDRRMP) current, approved by Sanggunian, aligned with NDRRMP 2020-2030 and Sendai Framework  \n  *Basis:* RA 10121 Sec. 12(c)(6); NDRRMP 2020-2030\n- **A3.2** (M, weight 2) DRR-CCA mainstreamed in CDP, CLUP, ELA and LCCAP (hazard data used in land use and investment decisions)  \n  *Basis:* RA 10121 Sec. 2; RA 9729 as amended by RA 10174; HLURB/DHSUD CLUP guidelines\n- **A3.3** (M, weight 3) Hazard-specific Contingency Plans for priority hazards (flood/flash flood, landslide, earthquake/tsunami, tropical cyclone, industrial/geothermal), updated and tested  \n  *Basis:* NDRRMC CP guidelines; OCD CP Manual\n- **A3.4** (M, weight 2) Public Service Continuity Plan (PSCP) prepared covering CDRRMO and essential city services  \n  *Basis:* NDRRMC/OCD PSCP Guidebook\n- **A3.7** (GP, weight 2) Barangay DRRM plans (85 barangays) reviewed/consolidated by CDRRMO  \n  *Basis:* RA 10121 Sec. 12(c)(6); DILG MC on BDRRM\n- **A5.1** (M, weight 3) Updated hazard maps for all priority hazards (MGB, PHIVOLCS, PAGASA, GeoRiskPH/HazardHunterPH) at barangay scale  \n  *Basis:* RA 10121 Sec. 12(c)(3); NDRRMP\n- **A5.2** (M, weight 3) Climate & Disaster Risk Assessment (CDRA)/ CRA completed with exposure (population, buildings, critical facilities) and vulnerability data  \n  *Basis:* DHSUD/CCC CDRA guidelines; RA 10121 Sec. 12(c)(3)\n- **A5.3** (M, weight 2) Disaggregated population database (sex, age, disability, IP, pregnant/lactating) for at-risk households  \n  *Basis:* RA 10121 Sec. 12(c)(5); RA 9710; RA 7277 as amended; RA 10821\n- **A5.8** (GP, weight 2) Critical facilities list (EOC, hospitals, evacuation centers, water, power, telecom, bridges, port) with dependencies mapped as potential failure chains and used to set protection and restoration priorities  \n  *Basis:* UNDRR DRSC 2.3.1; RA 12287 IRR (2026) Rule I Sec. 5(b),(d)\n- **A6.6** (GP, weight 1) IEC program on hazards and preparedness with annual reach targets  \n  *Basis:* RA 10121 Sec. 12(c)(13)\n- **A7.1** (M, weight 2) Annual training program for city personnel, BDRRMCs, schools and communities implemented  \n  *Basis:* RA 10121 Sec. 12(c)(12), Sec. 14\n- **A7.2** (M, weight 2) Participation in quarterly Nationwide Simultaneous Earthquake Drill (NSED) and hazard-specific drills with evaluation  \n  *Basis:* NDRRMC NSED guidelines\n- **A7.3** (GP, weight 2) BDRRMC functionality across 85 barangays assessed (e.g., Listo si KAP) with support plan for low-functioning barangays  \n  *Basis:* RA 10121; DILG MC 2025-035 (Listo si KAP)\n- **A7.6** (M, weight 2) Inclusive DRRM: GAD, PWD, senior citizen, children, IP considerations embedded in plans and services, with vulnerable-sector representatives confirming they were engaged  \n  *Basis:* RA 9710; RA 7277 as amended; RA 9994; RA 10821; RA 8371; RA 12287 IRR (2026) Rule IV Sec. 1(a); UNDRR DRSC 7.2.2\n- **A7.7** (GP, weight 1) Schools, hospitals and critical facilities included in preparedness planning and drills  \n  *Basis:* DepEd/DOH DRRM policies; Safe Schools/Hospitals\n- **A7.8** (GP, weight 1) Refresher cycle (at least annual) set for trained responders, EOC staff and BDRRMC members, with attendance tracked  \n  *Basis:* UNDRR DRSC 6.4.2\n- **C1.1** (GP, weight 2) Most-probable and most-severe risk scenarios inform CDP/CLUP priorities and the location of major investments  \n  *Basis:* UNDRR DRSC 1.1.1; RA 10121 Sec. 2; DHSUD CLUP guidelines\n- **C1.2** (GP, weight 1) DRR/CCA screening step in project and budget approval (LDC, LFC)  \n  *Basis:* UNDRR DRSC 1.3.1; climate change expenditure tagging guidelines\n- **C1.3** (GP, weight 1) CDRA estimates losses beyond physical assets: livelihoods and jobs, housing and displacement, agriculture, ecosystems, cultural heritage  \n  *Basis:* UNDRR DRSC 2.2.2; DHSUD/CCC CDRA guidelines\n- **C1.4** (GP, weight 2) Risk-sensitive development guidelines applied in zoning and building permits, based on hazard maps  \n  *Basis:* UNDRR DRSC 2.4.1; CLUP/ZO\n- **C3.1** (GP, weight 2) Critical protective ecosystems (upper Anilao-Malbasag watershed, upland forest cover, coastal mangroves) identified and monitored as risk-reduction assets  \n  *Basis:* UNDRR DRSC 5.1.1; RA 9729 as amended','Generated from IAT v1.1','draft'),
('1008c58c-bb8c-5cab-82ec-2e441910ae6b'::uuid,'eafa0947-d859-57e8-b93e-affd8500f0a5'::uuid,'v0.1 skeleton',E'# MOO Ch.4 – Operations, Warning and Response\n\n> Skeleton generated from IAT v1.1. Replace each requirement with the City''s procedure, standard or form.\n\n## Requirements this section must meet\n\n- **A2.5** (M, weight 3) 24/7 operations capability with documented shift roster (Operations Center/Duty officers)  \n  *Basis:* RA 10121 Sec. 12(c)(16); EOC guidelines\n- **A2.7** (M, weight 2) Personnel welfare and safety: insurance, hazard pay, PPE, psychosocial support for responders  \n  *Basis:* RA 10121 Sec. 12; RA 11036 (MHPSS); CSC rules\n- **A3.6** (M, weight 3) Evacuation plan with mapped routes, safe zones, centers and pre-emptive evacuation triggers per barangay  \n  *Basis:* RA 10121; RA 12076; DILG Operation L!sto\n- **A6.1** (M, weight 3) Hazard-specific EWS operational for flood (incl. Anilao/Malbasag river systems), rain-induced landslide, tsunami (Ormoc Bay) and tropical cyclone  \n  *Basis:* RA 10121 Sec. 12(c)(8); PAGASA/PHIVOLCS protocols\n- **A6.3** (M, weight 3) Last-mile dissemination channels tested to barangay/purok level (sirens, radio, SMS/ECBS, social media, barangay criers)  \n  *Basis:* RA 10639 (Free Mobile Disaster Alerts); NDRRMC EWS\n- **A6.4** (GP, weight 2) Warnings issued in local language (Cebuano/ Ormocanon) and accessible formats (sign language, visual alerts for PWD)  \n  *Basis:* RA 10121; RA 11106 (FSL Act); RA 7277\n- **A6.7** (M, weight 2) Templates and channels for public notice of a State of Imminent Disaster and of the anticipatory actions required, incl. sector-specific impact-based advisories and reach to geographically isolated barangays  \n  *Basis:* RA 12287 IRR (2026) Rule IV Sec. 2\n- **A7.4** (M, weight 3) Permanent evacuation center(s) planned/established and existing ECs meet minimum standards (WASH, privacy, PWD access, child-friendly space)  \n  *Basis:* RA 12076 (Ligtas Pinoy Centers Act); RA 10821; DSWD standards\n- **A7.6** (M, weight 2) Inclusive DRRM: GAD, PWD, senior citizen, children, IP considerations embedded in plans and services, with vulnerable-sector representatives confirming they were engaged  \n  *Basis:* RA 9710; RA 7277 as amended; RA 9994; RA 10821; RA 8371; RA 12287 IRR (2026) Rule IV Sec. 1(a); UNDRR DRSC 7.2.2\n- **A7.9** (GP, weight 2) BDRRMCs can account for residents of affected puroks within 12 hours of impact (welfare check), shown in a drill or a real event  \n  *Basis:* UNDRR DRSC 7.2.1\n- **A8.1** (M, weight 3) Incident Command System institutionalized: EO on ICS, trained IMT roster, pre-designated Incident Commanders  \n  *Basis:* NDRRMC MC No. 4, s. 2012 (ICS)\n- **A8.2** (M, weight 3) Organized and trained response teams: SAR (WASAR/CSSR/HAZMAT as relevant), EMS/ambulance, fire coordination with BFP  \n  *Basis:* RA 10121 Sec. 12(c)(16); RA 11589 (BFP)\n- **A8.3** (M, weight 2) Response equipment and vehicles inventoried, serviceable and maintained (preventive maintenance schedule)  \n  *Basis:* COA property rules; RA 10121\n- **A8.7** (M, weight 2) Management of the Dead and Missing (MDM) and Rapid Damage Assessment & Needs Analysis (RDANA) teams designated and trained  \n  *Basis:* NDRRMC MDM & RDANA guidelines\n- **A8.8** (M, weight 3) Anticipatory action protocols by hazard and lead time: office-order templates for prepositioning (relief, medical supplies, animal feed, water and power for evacuation centers), deployment of heavy equipment, transport and personnel, pre-emptive evacuation incl. livestock and pets, CCCM, and safeguarding of critical infrastructure; aligned with CPs, Oplan L!sto and evacuation plans  \n  *Basis:* RA 12287 IRR (2026) Rule IV Secs. 1, 3, 4, 6\n- **A8.9** (M, weight 2) Anticipatory social amelioration: families identified and prioritized using CBMS or the prevailing registry; data-sharing agreements compliant with RA 10173; local guidelines for anticipatory cash or vouchers issued with the CSWDO  \n  *Basis:* RA 12287 IRR (2026) Rule IV Sec. 7; RA 11315 (CBMS); RA 10173\n- **C2.1** (GP, weight 3) Structural safety of the EOC, evacuation centers and critical public facilities assessed by the Building Official, with a rapid safety inspection procedure before forecast impact  \n  *Basis:* UNDRR DRSC 4.3.1, 4.4.2; PD 1096; RA 12076; RA 12287 IRR (2026) Rule IV Sec. 4(c)(i)','Generated from IAT v1.1','draft'),
('6cc001df-e80d-5b30-a27d-30dc304285a3'::uuid,'d7190e43-31f8-55d7-b646-04574073dedf'::uuid,'v0.1 skeleton',E'# MOO Ch.5 – Recovery, Rehabilitation and Build Back Better\n\n> Skeleton generated from IAT v1.1. Replace each requirement with the City''s procedure, standard or form.\n\n## Requirements this section must meet\n\n- **A9.1** (GP, weight 2) Post-Disaster Needs Assessment (PDNA) capacity: trained team and templates ready  \n  *Basis:* NDRRMC PDNA guidelines; OCD\n- **A9.2** (M, weight 2) Rehabilitation & recovery plan prepared after major events, with build-back-better and resettlement provisions  \n  *Basis:* RA 10121 Sec. 12(c)(11); NDRRMP Pillar 4\n- **A9.3** (GP, weight 1) Recovery data (damage, losses, livelihood, housing) tracked to completion  \n  *Basis:* Sendai Framework targets C-D\n- **A9.4** (GP, weight 1) Psychosocial and livelihood recovery services coordinated with CSWDO, CHO, PESO  \n  *Basis:* RA 11036; DSWD protocols\n- **A9.5** (GP, weight 2) Pre-disaster recovery framework: roles, PDNA activation, temporary shelter, debris management and recovery fund sources agreed before an event  \n  *Basis:* UNDRR DRSC Essential 10; NDRRMP Pillar 4','Generated from IAT v1.1','draft'),
('ea2c5737-7918-5543-ac50-e7b037af5d62'::uuid,'d61fc0e9-7136-5375-ab68-40132bc8dd3c'::uuid,'v0.1 skeleton',E'# MOO Ch.6 – DRRM Financing, Resource Management and Accountability\n\n> Skeleton generated from IAT v1.1. Replace each requirement with the City''s procedure, standard or form.\n\n## Requirements this section must meet\n\n- **A3.5** (M, weight 3) Annual LDRRMF Investment Plan (LDRRMFIP) prepared, approved and consistent with LDRRMP  \n  *Basis:* JMC 2013-1\n- **A4.1** (M, weight 3) LDRRMF set at not less than 5% of estimated revenue from regular sources  \n  *Basis:* RA 10121 Sec. 21; JMC 2013-1\n- **A4.2** (M, weight 3) 70% Mitigation/Preparedness and 30% Quick Response Fund (QRF) allocation observed  \n  *Basis:* RA 10121 Sec. 21; JMC 2013-1\n- **A4.3** (M, weight 2) Unexpended LDRRMF transferred to Special Trust Fund and used within 5 years  \n  *Basis:* RA 10121 Sec. 21; COA Circular 2012-002\n- **A4.4** (GP, weight 2) LDRRMF utilization rate monitored and reported (target >= 80% of current-year 70% fund)  \n  *Basis:* JMC 2013-1; COA AAR findings\n- **A4.5** (M, weight 2) Emergency procurement procedures (negotiated procurement - emergency cases) documented and pre-arranged (framework agreements, pre-qualified suppliers)  \n  *Basis:* RA 12009 (New Government Procurement Act) & IRR\n- **A4.6** (M, weight 2) Anticipatory action funding pathway: LDRRMFIP sets an AA line within the cap of 10% of the 70% LDRRMF; other sources mapped (Special Trust Fund balances, donations, ODA); Budget, Accounting and BAC procedures allow immediate disbursement and observe the 30%/70% tranche rule around the 3-day lead time  \n  *Basis:* RA 12287; RA 12287 IRR (2026) Rule V Secs. 1-3; RA 10121 Sec. 21; RA 12009\n- **A4.7** (GP, weight 1) Risk transfer/financing instruments explored (indemnity insurance of public assets, PSF access, partnerships)  \n  *Basis:* NDRRMP; RA 10174 (People''s Survival Fund); DOF-BTr NIP\n- **A4.8** (M, weight 2) Clean COA findings on LDRRMF in last audit year (or findings addressed)  \n  *Basis:* COA Circular 2012-002\n- **A4.9** (GP, weight 2) QRF and LDRRMF adequacy tested against the most severe credible scenario (e.g., a Thelma-type flash flood or Yolanda-strength typhoon), with the shortfall and other fund sources identified  \n  *Basis:* UNDRR DRSC 3.2.3, 3.2.4; JMC 2013-1\n- **A10.5** (M, weight 1) Full Disclosure Policy: LDRRMF and utilization posted publicly  \n  *Basis:* DILG FDP MCs; RA 10121 Sec. 21\n- **C1.2** (GP, weight 1) DRR/CCA screening step in project and budget approval (LDC, LFC)  \n  *Basis:* UNDRR DRSC 1.3.1; climate change expenditure tagging guidelines','Generated from IAT v1.1','draft'),
('99af31ad-0c1a-52c6-970b-815d9b7fc0ff'::uuid,'aec20d50-301b-57ce-87d4-64154502a0ef'::uuid,'v0.1 skeleton',E'# MOO Ch.7 – Monitoring, Evaluation, Knowledge Management and Continuous Improvement\n\n> Skeleton generated from IAT v1.1. Replace each requirement with the City''s procedure, standard or form.\n\n## Requirements this section must meet\n\n- **A5.4** (GP, weight 2) DRRM information system/ database with disaster event history, damage and losses (incl. 1991 flood, 2013 Yolanda, 2017 earthquake records)  \n  *Basis:* RA 10121 Sec. 12(c)(5); Sendai monitoring\n- **A5.5** (M, weight 2) Data privacy compliance for beneficiary and affected-population data (DPO, consent, data sharing agreements)  \n  *Basis:* RA 10173 (Data Privacy Act); NPC circulars\n- **A5.6** (GP, weight 1) GIS capability (software, trained staff, updated base maps) within Research & Planning  \n  *Basis:* JMC 2014-1 (R&P functions)\n- **A5.7** (GP, weight 2) One maintained, shared source of risk and readiness information (hazard maps, plans, contacts, readiness summary) open to CDRRMC member offices, with a public summary posted  \n  *Basis:* UNDRR DRSC 1.4.1, 6.3.1, 6.3.2; RA 10173\n- **A5.9** (GP, weight 1) Agreed update cycle: hazard data every 3 years or less; exposure, vulnerability and critical-facility data every 18 months or less  \n  *Basis:* UNDRR DRSC 2.5.1\n- **A10.3** (M, weight 2) Regular reporting to OCD Region VIII/RDRRMC and DILG (SitReps, LDRRMF reports, Operation L!sto)  \n  *Basis:* RA 10121; DILG MCs\n- **A10.4** (M, weight 2) Monitoring & evaluation framework for LDRRMP with indicators and annual review  \n  *Basis:* RA 10121 Sec. 12(c)(6)\n- **A10.6** (GP, weight 2) After-action reviews conducted after significant events and lessons integrated into plans  \n  *Basis:* NDRRMC; good practice\n- **A10.7** (GP, weight 1) Participation in performance recognition/assessment systems (Gawad KALASAG Seal, SGLG Disaster Preparedness) and gaps acted upon  \n  *Basis:* NDRRMC GKS guidelines; RA 11292 (SGLG Act)\n- **A10.8** (M, weight 2) Post-declaration report within 45 days of lifting a State of Imminent Disaster (declaration status, AA fund utilization, estimated economic and social costs minimized); reporting route confirmed with OCD VIII  \n  *Basis:* RA 12287 IRR (2026) Rule VI Sec. 1\n- **A10.9** (GP, weight 1) Structured learning from other LGUs and networks (exchanges, OCD forums, MCR2030), with resulting changes documented  \n  *Basis:* UNDRR DRSC 6.6.1','Generated from IAT v1.1','draft'),
('955f1841-625f-5638-a229-7b93c39869e2'::uuid,'cb5fb5fd-5044-57b7-84fe-dff921b0c759'::uuid,'v0.1 skeleton',E'# MOO Ch.8 – Stakeholder Engagement and Institutional Partnerships\n\n> Skeleton generated from IAT v1.1. Replace each requirement with the City''s procedure, standard or form.\n\n## Requirements this section must meet\n\n- **A10.1** (GP, weight 2) MOAs/ mutual aid agreements with neighbouring LGUs (Kananga, Albuera, Merida, Isabel etc.) and Province of Leyte  \n  *Basis:* RA 10121 Sec. 12(c)(15); RA 7160 Sec. 33\n- **A10.2** (GP, weight 1) Partnerships with CSOs, private sector (incl. energy/geothermal operators), academe and faith-based groups documented, with pre- and post-event roles defined and at least annual coordination meetings  \n  *Basis:* RA 10121 Sec. 12(c)(15); UNDRR DRSC 6.1.2, 6.1.4\n- **C2.2** (GP, weight 2) Pre-crisis and priority-restoration arrangements with power, water and telecom providers (load-shedding and water-rationing plans, cell-on-wheels, restoration priority list)  \n  *Basis:* UNDRR DRSC Essential 8; RA 12287 IRR (2026) Rule IV Sec. 4(c)(ii)-(iv)\n- **C3.2** (GP, weight 1) Arrangements with neighbouring LGUs and DENR where watersheds or protective ecosystems extend beyond city limits  \n  *Basis:* UNDRR DRSC 5.3.1, 5.3.2; RA 7160 Sec. 33\n- **C5.1** (GP, weight 1) Business continuity outreach to local businesses based on shared hazard scenarios (outreach only; no mandate implied)  \n  *Basis:* UNDRR DRSC 7.3.2','Generated from IAT v1.1','draft'),
('8c4febb5-60d9-575e-a8ef-113012d3083d'::uuid,'154dc4f3-6d53-5aec-82d7-474fc6d004b1'::uuid,'v0.1 skeleton',E'# EOC Ch.1 – Legal Basis\n\n> Skeleton generated from IAT v1.1. Replace each requirement with the City''s procedure, standard or form.\n\n## Requirements this section must meet\n\n- **B1.1** (M, weight 3) EOC established by EO/ordinance with defined mandate, authority and relationship to CDRRMC and ICS  \n  *Basis:* NDRRMC Memorandum No. 131, s. 2018 (EOC Guidelines); RA 10121\n- **B7.1** (M, weight 3) Written EOC SOPs/ Manual approved and disseminated to all EOC staff  \n  *Basis:* NDRRMC EOC Guidelines','Generated from IAT v1.1','draft'),
('098330dc-3302-5bf2-92e7-2e41e9d2ae8e'::uuid,'33665e28-8c73-5cda-912b-4ddcf179ea16'::uuid,'v0.1 skeleton',E'# EOC Ch.2 – Concept of Operations and Activation\n\n> Skeleton generated from IAT v1.1. Replace each requirement with the City''s procedure, standard or form.\n\n## Requirements this section must meet\n\n- **A1.8** (M, weight 3) State of Imminent Disaster procedure: CDRRMC coordinates with RDRRMC VIII when the pre-disaster risk assessment shows reasonable certainty of severe impact; request format to RDRRMC (24-hour reply); Mayor''s EO template; adoption rule when the Region (or Province, applicability to an ICC to be confirmed) is declared; lifting grounds and authority  \n  *Basis:* RA 12287; RA 12287 IRR (2026) Rule II Sec. 6; Rule III Secs. 2-4\n- **A6.2** (M, weight 3) Warning thresholds linked to specific actions (alert levels -> pre-emptive evacuation, class/work suspension, State of Imminent Disaster request) in written protocols, built to take up NDRRMC impact-based triggers once issued  \n  *Basis:* RA 10121; RA 12287; RA 12287 IRR (2026) Rule II Sec. 2; DILG Operation L!sto\n- **A8.6** (M, weight 3) Pre-Disaster Risk Assessment (PDRA) conducted before forecast hazards, with anticipatory actions recorded  \n  *Basis:* NDRRMC PDRA protocol; RA 12287; RA 12287 IRR (2026) Rule II Sec. 5\n- **A8.8** (M, weight 3) Anticipatory action protocols by hazard and lead time: office-order templates for prepositioning (relief, medical supplies, animal feed, water and power for evacuation centers), deployment of heavy equipment, transport and personnel, pre-emptive evacuation incl. livestock and pets, CCCM, and safeguarding of critical infrastructure; aligned with CPs, Oplan L!sto and evacuation plans  \n  *Basis:* RA 12287 IRR (2026) Rule IV Secs. 1, 3, 4, 6\n- **B1.2** (M, weight 3) Alert/activation levels defined (e.g., White-normal, Blue-alert, Red-full activation) with hazard-based triggers and a defined EOC posture when a State of Imminent Disaster is declared  \n  *Basis:* National Disaster Response Plan; RDRRMC VIII Res. No. 12-006, s. 2023; NDRRMC Memorandum No. 131, s. 2018; RA 12287 IRR (2026) Rule IV Sec. 1\n- **B1.3** (M, weight 3) Activation, escalation, de-escalation and deactivation procedures with designated authority  \n  *Basis:* NDRRMC EOC Guidelines\n- **B1.4** (M, weight 2) Concept of operations documents EOC functions: coordination, information management, resource management, policy support  \n  *Basis:* NDRRMC EOC Guidelines\n- **B1.5** (M, weight 2) EOC linkage to Provincial (Leyte) and Regional (OCD VIII) EOCs defined  \n  *Basis:* NDRRMC EOC Guidelines\n- **B7.1** (M, weight 3) Written EOC SOPs/ Manual approved and disseminated to all EOC staff  \n  *Basis:* NDRRMC EOC Guidelines\n- **C3.3** (GP, weight 2) Environmental anticipatory actions: declogging of waterways and drainage, slope stabilization, safe debris and carcass disposal  \n  *Basis:* RA 12287 IRR (2026) Rule IV Sec. 10(d)','Generated from IAT v1.1','draft'),
('bb994eca-e94d-50ac-9768-86d6527a9735'::uuid,'81fe614e-15e5-516a-9f84-8f033aec5526'::uuid,'v0.1 skeleton',E'# EOC Ch.3 – Facility, Site and Continuity\n\n> Skeleton generated from IAT v1.1. Replace each requirement with the City''s procedure, standard or form.\n\n## Requirements this section must meet\n\n- **A3.3** (M, weight 3) Hazard-specific Contingency Plans for priority hazards (flood/flash flood, landslide, earthquake/tsunami, tropical cyclone, industrial/geothermal), updated and tested  \n  *Basis:* NDRRMC CP guidelines; OCD CP Manual\n- **A3.6** (M, weight 3) Evacuation plan with mapped routes, safe zones, centers and pre-emptive evacuation triggers per barangay  \n  *Basis:* RA 10121; RA 12076; DILG Operation L!sto\n- **A5.8** (GP, weight 2) Critical facilities list (EOC, hospitals, evacuation centers, water, power, telecom, bridges, port) with dependencies mapped as potential failure chains and used to set protection and restoration priorities  \n  *Basis:* UNDRR DRSC 2.3.1; RA 12287 IRR (2026) Rule I Sec. 5(b),(d)\n- **A6.1** (M, weight 3) Hazard-specific EWS operational for flood (incl. Anilao/Malbasag river systems), rain-induced landslide, tsunami (Ormoc Bay) and tropical cyclone  \n  *Basis:* RA 10121 Sec. 12(c)(8); PAGASA/PHIVOLCS protocols\n- **B2.1** (M, weight 3) EOC site located outside high flood, landslide, tsunami and liquefaction zones (checked vs hazard maps)  \n  *Basis:* NDRRMC EOC Guidelines; hazard maps\n- **B2.2** (M, weight 3) Building structural integrity assessed (seismic - Philippine Fault proximity) and certified  \n  *Basis:* NBC (PD 1096); NSCP; DPWH\n- **B2.3** (M, weight 3) Backup power (generator + fuel for >=72 hours, UPS) tested regularly  \n  *Basis:* NDRRMC EOC Guidelines; good practice\n- **B2.4** (GP, weight 2) Functional layout: operations floor, briefing/decision room, comms room, rest area, sanitation, kitchen  \n  *Basis:* NDRRMC EOC Guidelines\n- **B2.5** (GP, weight 1) Water, food and sanitation supplies for EOC staff for >=72 hours  \n  *Basis:* Good practice; PSCP\n- **B2.6** (GP, weight 1) Physical security and access control (ID, visitor log, CCTV)  \n  *Basis:* Good practice\n- **B2.7** (M, weight 2) Designated and equipped alternate EOC with relocation procedure  \n  *Basis:* PSCP Guidebook; NDRRMC EOC Guidelines\n- **B7.1** (M, weight 3) Written EOC SOPs/ Manual approved and disseminated to all EOC staff  \n  *Basis:* NDRRMC EOC Guidelines\n- **C2.1** (GP, weight 3) Structural safety of the EOC, evacuation centers and critical public facilities assessed by the Building Official, with a rapid safety inspection procedure before forecast impact  \n  *Basis:* UNDRR DRSC 4.3.1, 4.4.2; PD 1096; RA 12076; RA 12287 IRR (2026) Rule IV Sec. 4(c)(i)','Generated from IAT v1.1','draft'),
('59b61309-18d9-583e-b87b-4e369fd494bc'::uuid,'613139e9-8daa-5fb3-b4a4-a8a8dc45b04c'::uuid,'v0.1 skeleton',E'# EOC Ch.4 – Communications and Sector Coordination\n\n> Skeleton generated from IAT v1.1. Replace each requirement with the City''s procedure, standard or form.\n\n## Requirements this section must meet\n\n- **A2.5** (M, weight 3) 24/7 operations capability with documented shift roster (Operations Center/Duty officers)  \n  *Basis:* RA 10121 Sec. 12(c)(16); EOC guidelines\n- **A8.4** (GP, weight 2) Emergency hotline integrated with E911 and dispatch protocol (call-taking to dispatch time tracked)  \n  *Basis:* EO 56 s. 2018 (E911); DILG guidelines\n- **A8.5** (M, weight 2) Response clusters organized at city level mirroring national cluster approach (Food & NFI, Health, WASH, CCCM, Logistics, Search Rescue & Retrieval, Law & Order, Education, Protection, ETC, MDM)  \n  *Basis:* NDCC MC No. 12, s. 2008; NDRRM Plan Response pillar\n- **B3.1** (M, weight 3) Redundant communications: VHF/UHF radio, HF, satellite phone, landline, mobile, internet (min. 3 independent channels)  \n  *Basis:* NDRRMC EOC Guidelines; NTC frequency assignment\n- **B3.2** (M, weight 2) Radio network covering all 85 barangays and responders, with call signs and net-control procedure  \n  *Basis:* NTC licensing; ETC cluster\n- **B3.3** (GP, weight 2) Backup internet (secondary ISP/satellite) and continuity of digital systems  \n  *Basis:* Good practice; DICT\n- **B3.4** (M, weight 2) Communications plan/ directory (agencies, barangays, clusters) updated within last 6 months  \n  *Basis:* NDRRMC EOC Guidelines\n- **B3.5** (GP, weight 1) Cybersecurity and information security measures for EOC systems  \n  *Basis:* RA 10173; DICT National Cybersecurity Plan\n- **B3.6** (GP, weight 1) Display and monitoring equipment (video wall/monitors, weather feeds, CCTV feeds)  \n  *Basis:* Good practice\n- **B7.1** (M, weight 3) Written EOC SOPs/ Manual approved and disseminated to all EOC staff  \n  *Basis:* NDRRMC EOC Guidelines\n- **C4.1** (GP, weight 3) Health anticipatory action: Health Cluster activation, facility service-continuity and surge plans, prepositioned commodities, health emergency response teams on standby  \n  *Basis:* RA 12287 IRR (2026) Rule IV Sec. 9\n- **C4.2** (GP, weight 2) Education anticipatory action: schools'' AA plans and learning-continuity modalities  \n  *Basis:* RA 12287 IRR (2026) Rule IV Sec. 10(a); RA 10821\n- **C4.3** (GP, weight 2) Agri-fisheries anticipatory action using RSBSA, FishR and livestock registries; early action guidelines on storage, inputs and animal health  \n  *Basis:* RA 12287 IRR (2026) Rule IV Sec. 8\n- **C4.4** (GP, weight 1) Pre-impact price monitoring and anti-profiteering of basic goods  \n  *Basis:* RA 12287 IRR (2026) Rule IV Sec. 10(c); RA 7581 (Price Act)','Generated from IAT v1.1','draft'),
('4b32eccb-7345-5f36-9f7d-69995cc9217c'::uuid,'9cd07e9f-bfa7-543a-9c6e-f56c433380de'::uuid,'v0.1 skeleton',E'# EOC Ch.5 – Organization, Staffing and Public Information\n\n> Skeleton generated from IAT v1.1. Replace each requirement with the City''s procedure, standard or form.\n\n## Requirements this section must meet\n\n- **A5.1** (M, weight 3) Updated hazard maps for all priority hazards (MGB, PHIVOLCS, PAGASA, GeoRiskPH/HazardHunterPH) at barangay scale  \n  *Basis:* RA 10121 Sec. 12(c)(3); NDRRMP\n- **A5.3** (M, weight 2) Disaggregated population database (sex, age, disability, IP, pregnant/lactating) for at-risk households  \n  *Basis:* RA 10121 Sec. 12(c)(5); RA 9710; RA 7277 as amended; RA 10821\n- **A6.5** (GP, weight 1) Designated public information officer and risk communication plan (incl. rumor/misinformation management)  \n  *Basis:* NDRRMC public info protocols\n- **A6.7** (M, weight 2) Templates and channels for public notice of a State of Imminent Disaster and of the anticipatory actions required, incl. sector-specific impact-based advisories and reach to geographically isolated barangays  \n  *Basis:* RA 12287 IRR (2026) Rule IV Sec. 2\n- **A10.3** (M, weight 2) Regular reporting to OCD Region VIII/RDRRMC and DILG (SitReps, LDRRMF reports, Operation L!sto)  \n  *Basis:* RA 10121; DILG MCs\n- **A10.8** (M, weight 2) Post-declaration report within 45 days of lifting a State of Imminent Disaster (declaration status, AA fund utilization, estimated economic and social costs minimized); reporting route confirmed with OCD VIII  \n  *Basis:* RA 12287 IRR (2026) Rule VI Sec. 1\n- **B4.1** (M, weight 3) EOC organizational structure defined (EOC Manager, Operations, Planning/Information, Logistics, Admin/Finance, liaison desks)  \n  *Basis:* NDRRMC EOC Guidelines; ICS\n- **B4.2** (M, weight 3) Pre-designated EOC staff with alternates (at least 2 deep per key position)  \n  *Basis:* NDRRMC EOC Guidelines\n- **B4.3** (M, weight 2) Duty roster for sustained 24/7 operations with shift handover protocol  \n  *Basis:* Good practice\n- **B4.4** (M, weight 2) Agency/cluster liaison desks identified (CSWDO, CHO, CEO, PNP, BFP, AFP, DepEd, utilities, Red Cross)  \n  *Basis:* NDCC MC 12 s. 2008; EOC Guidelines\n- **B4.5** (GP, weight 2) Position checklists/job action sheets for each EOC role  \n  *Basis:* Good practice\n- **B4.6** (GP, weight 1) Responder welfare in EOC: rest cycles, meals, MHPSS, family support  \n  *Basis:* RA 11036; good practice\n- **B7.1** (M, weight 3) Written EOC SOPs/ Manual approved and disseminated to all EOC staff  \n  *Basis:* NDRRMC EOC Guidelines','Generated from IAT v1.1','draft'),
('f7ab1636-e4a2-5bd3-b710-eb5b1d5d1a22'::uuid,'a0cad148-d5ee-5805-bf81-4b86fbf1aeac'::uuid,'v0.1 skeleton',E'# EOC Ch.6 – Information Management and Reporting\n\n> Skeleton generated from IAT v1.1. Replace each requirement with the City''s procedure, standard or form.\n\n## Requirements this section must meet\n\n- **A4.5** (M, weight 2) Emergency procurement procedures (negotiated procurement - emergency cases) documented and pre-arranged (framework agreements, pre-qualified suppliers)  \n  *Basis:* RA 12009 (New Government Procurement Act) & IRR\n- **A7.4** (M, weight 3) Permanent evacuation center(s) planned/established and existing ECs meet minimum standards (WASH, privacy, PWD access, child-friendly space)  \n  *Basis:* RA 12076 (Ligtas Pinoy Centers Act); RA 10821; DSWD standards\n- **A7.5** (M, weight 2) Prepositioned relief stocks/food packs and non-food items with inventory and replenishment triggers  \n  *Basis:* RA 10121; DSWD-LGU protocols; Operation L!sto\n- **A7.9** (GP, weight 2) BDRRMCs can account for residents of affected puroks within 12 hours of impact (welfare check), shown in a drill or a real event  \n  *Basis:* UNDRR DRSC 7.2.1\n- **A8.3** (M, weight 2) Response equipment and vehicles inventoried, serviceable and maintained (preventive maintenance schedule)  \n  *Basis:* COA property rules; RA 10121\n- **A10.1** (GP, weight 2) MOAs/ mutual aid agreements with neighbouring LGUs (Kananga, Albuera, Merida, Isabel etc.) and Province of Leyte  \n  *Basis:* RA 10121 Sec. 12(c)(15); RA 7160 Sec. 33\n- **B5.1** (M, weight 3) Standard SitRep/ Report templates aligned with NDRRMC/OCD formats and fixed reporting schedule  \n  *Basis:* NDRRMC reporting protocol\n- **B5.2** (M, weight 3) Barangay-to-city reporting flow (BDRRMC -> EOC) with defined timelines and formats  \n  *Basis:* RA 10121; DILG\n- **B5.3** (GP, weight 2) Common Operating Picture maintained (dashboard/ GIS map of incidents, evacuees, resources)  \n  *Basis:* NDRRMC EOC Guidelines\n- **B5.4** (M, weight 2) Evacuation center and affected-family tracking (DAFAC/ registration) feeds EOC data  \n  *Basis:* DSWD DAFAC; RA 10821\n- **B5.5** (M, weight 2) EOC logbook/ significant events log and document retention  \n  *Basis:* Good practice; NAP rules\n- **B5.6** (M, weight 2) Weather/hazard monitoring routine (PAGASA, PHIVOLCS feeds) with bulletins logged and disseminated  \n  *Basis:* RA 10121; PAGASA protocols\n- **B5.7** (GP, weight 1) Inbound citizen reporting (hotline, SMS, social media) feeds the common operating picture after a verification step  \n  *Basis:* UNDRR DRSC 7.4.2\n- **B7.1** (M, weight 3) Written EOC SOPs/ Manual approved and disseminated to all EOC staff  \n  *Basis:* NDRRMC EOC Guidelines','Generated from IAT v1.1','draft'),
('6f2e209c-33ef-5ac6-bcc3-99c5096980b3'::uuid,'f3002288-2f46-522f-911e-0fc6aa0b6afe'::uuid,'v0.1 skeleton',E'# EOC Ch.7 – Coordination and Resource Management\n\n> Skeleton generated from IAT v1.1. Replace each requirement with the City''s procedure, standard or form.\n\n## Requirements this section must meet\n\n- **A3.4** (M, weight 2) Public Service Continuity Plan (PSCP) prepared covering CDRRMO and essential city services  \n  *Basis:* NDRRMC/OCD PSCP Guidebook\n- **B2.7** (M, weight 2) Designated and equipped alternate EOC with relocation procedure  \n  *Basis:* PSCP Guidebook; NDRRMC EOC Guidelines\n- **B6.1** (M, weight 3) ICS-EOC interface defined: EOC supports Incident Commander(s); no duplication of command  \n  *Basis:* NDRRMC MC No. 4 s. 2012; EOC Guidelines\n- **B6.2** (M, weight 3) Resource management system: request, tracking, mobilization and demobilization of resources  \n  *Basis:* ICS resource management; EOC Guidelines\n- **B6.3** (M, weight 2) Resource inventory (city, barangays, partners, private sector) accessible from EOC  \n  *Basis:* RA 10121; ICS\n- **B6.4** (GP, weight 1) Procedures for receiving and managing external assistance/ donations and volunteers  \n  *Basis:* NDRRMC guidelines on international/ external assistance\n- **B6.5** (GP, weight 2) Decision-support briefings to CDRRMC/Mayor at fixed intervals during activation  \n  *Basis:* EOC Guidelines\n- **B6.6** (GP, weight 2) Pre-arranged resource commitments from partners and suppliers set out by item, quantity, activation trigger and contact in signed agreements (incl. supplier agreements tapped for anticipatory action)  \n  *Basis:* UNDRR DRSC 1.2.4; RA 12287 IRR (2026) Rule IV Sec. 6(a)(ii)\n- **B7.1** (M, weight 3) Written EOC SOPs/ Manual approved and disseminated to all EOC staff  \n  *Basis:* NDRRMC EOC Guidelines\n- **C2.2** (GP, weight 2) Pre-crisis and priority-restoration arrangements with power, water and telecom providers (load-shedding and water-rationing plans, cell-on-wheels, restoration priority list)  \n  *Basis:* UNDRR DRSC Essential 8; RA 12287 IRR (2026) Rule IV Sec. 4(c)(ii)-(iv)\n- **C2.3** (GP, weight 2) Transport anticipatory actions: pre-inspection of bridges, alternate routes and traffic teams, coordination with seaport and terminal operators  \n  *Basis:* UNDRR DRSC Essential 8; RA 12287 IRR (2026) Rule IV Sec. 10(b)','Generated from IAT v1.1','draft'),
('890fcbd5-6c8a-5e82-b573-37f10db30d85'::uuid,'b565a903-0418-5524-9c0d-3839f503cacd'::uuid,'v0.1 skeleton',E'# EOC Ch.8 – Training and Exercises\n\n> Skeleton generated from IAT v1.1. Replace each requirement with the City''s procedure, standard or form.\n\n## Requirements this section must meet\n\n- **B7.1** (M, weight 3) Written EOC SOPs/ Manual approved and disseminated to all EOC staff  \n  *Basis:* NDRRMC EOC Guidelines\n- **B7.2** (M, weight 2) EOC staff trained (EOC operations course, ICS, IM) with records  \n  *Basis:* OCD/DRRM training; NDRRMC EOC Guidelines\n- **B7.3** (M, weight 2) Annual exercise program (tabletop, functional, full-scale) testing EOC activation  \n  *Basis:* NDRRMC; HSEEP-style good practice\n- **B7.4** (GP, weight 2) After-action review after each activation with improvement plan tracked  \n  *Basis:* Good practice','Generated from IAT v1.1','draft'),
('723c1671-a5c8-598b-b523-75fcdf5873e5'::uuid,'db682ca2-878b-59f5-9751-3d1a1d8dae79'::uuid,'v0.1 skeleton',E'# EOC Ch.9 – Sustainability\n\n> Skeleton generated from IAT v1.1. Replace each requirement with the City''s procedure, standard or form.\n\n## Requirements this section must meet\n\n- **B7.1** (M, weight 3) Written EOC SOPs/ Manual approved and disseminated to all EOC staff  \n  *Basis:* NDRRMC EOC Guidelines\n- **B7.5** (M, weight 2) Dedicated EOC budget for operations, maintenance and upgrades in LDRRMFIP  \n  *Basis:* JMC 2013-1\n- **B7.6** (GP, weight 1) Equipment maintenance schedule and annual EOC readiness self-check  \n  *Basis:* Good practice; PSCP','Generated from IAT v1.1','draft'),
('706d3315-068d-575b-814c-23e4e18a7f7e'::uuid,'4b930207-f0f5-5106-b657-d5057ebf28ad'::uuid,'v0.1 skeleton',E'# MOO Annex JDs – Job descriptions\n\n> Skeleton generated from IAT v1.1. Replace each requirement with the City''s procedure, standard or form.\n\n## Requirements this section must meet\n\n- **A2.4** (M, weight 2) Job descriptions/position descriptions defined for every position, aligned to RA 10121 functions  \n  *Basis:* CSC rules; JMC 2014-1','Generated from IAT v1.1','draft'),
('a197a7c7-622c-540e-b4d3-591d2db27aba'::uuid,'2108b48d-63ed-5be3-bdb5-2d1bdabb3811'::uuid,'v0.9 consolidated draft',E'# INSTITUTIONAL IMPLEMENTATION PACKAGE\n\nThis package gives operational effect to Chapter 1 through a coordinated set of proposed legislative and executive instruments, standard operating procedures, responsibility matrices and governance templates. It is an integrated annex set and must be read with Chapter 1, particularly Sections 6–8, 11–14.\n\n# DOCUMENT CONTROL AND APPROVAL\n\n| **Control field**         | **Designation / entry**                                | **Control field**             | **Designation / entry**           |\n|---------------------------|--------------------------------------------------------|-------------------------------|-----------------------------------|\n| **Document owner**        | CDRRMO Head                                            | **Document custodian**        | CDRRMO Secretariat                |\n| **Technical review**      | CDRRMO / EOC / concerned offices                       | **Legal review**              | City Legal Office                 |\n| **Administrative review** | HRMO / Budget / Accounting / BAC                       | **External technical review** | OCD Region VIII, as applicable    |\n| **Approval**              | Mayor / CDRRMC / Sanggunian, as legally applicable     | **Effective date**            | Upon valid approval / issuance    |\n| **Review cycle**          | Annual and upon material legal or institutional change | **Supersedes**                | None – initial consolidated draft |\n\n## Revision history\n\n| **Version** | **Date**    | **Description**                                                                                     | **Prepared / reviewed by**            |\n|-------------|-------------|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|---------------------------------------|\n| 0.9         | 31 Oct 2026 | Integrated working draft based on uploaded Chapter 1 and assessment-informed implementation package | Prepared for institutional validation |\n\nApproval status: This document is a controlled working draft. No provision becomes an official City policy, ordinance, executive order or operational directive until approved and issued by the authority legally competent to do so.\n\n# Annex register and cross-reference guide\n\n| **Annex** | **Instrument**                                               | **Approval / control route**           |\n|-----------|--------------------------------------------------------------|----------------------------------------|\n| 1-A       | Proposed CDRRMO institutionalization ordinance               | Sangguniang Panlungsod                 |\n| 1-B       | Proposed CDRRMC reconstitution Executive Order               | City Mayor                             |\n| 1-C       | Proposed EOC establishment Executive Order                   | City Mayor                             |\n| 1-D       | SOP GOV-04: State of Calamity declaration and lifting        | Approval under City delegation         |\n| 1-E       | SOP GOV-05: State of Imminent Disaster / anticipatory action | Approval after RA 12287 IRR validation |\n| 1-F       | Master RACI and institutional interface matrix               | CDRRMC / City approval                 |\n| 1-G       | Governance forms GOV-F01 to GOV-F16                          | CDRRMO Secretariat custodian           |\n\nConsistent definitions. CDRRMC means City Disaster Risk Reduction and Management Council; CDRRMO means permanent City Disaster Risk Reduction and Management Office; EOC means Emergency Operations Center as an operational coordination mechanism; ICS means Incident Command System; IMT means Incident Management Team; PDRA means Pre-Disaster Risk Assessment; RDANA means Rapid Damage Assessment and Needs Analysis. These definitions are descriptive and do not confer authority beyond applicable law.\n\nDocument hierarchy. Philippine statutes and valid implementing rules prevail over administrative issuances, local executive issuances, approved plans, SOPs and forms. RACI designations allocate work but do not create statutory powers or transfer mandates.\n','Chapter 1 consolidated draft v0.9 (31 Oct 2026)','draft')
